g minimal elements into maximal elements, or sources into sinks. We derive toric analogues for several features of ordinary partial orders, such as chains, antichains, transitivity, Hasse diagrams, linear extensions, and total orders.\nTropical hyperplane arrangements and oriented matroids\n\nPublished • View Publication • BIB\n\nWe study the combinatorial properties of a tropical hyperplane arrangement. We define tropical oriented matroids, and prove that they share many of the properties of ordinary oriented matroids. We show that a tropical oriented matroid determines a subdivision of a product of two simplices, and conjecture that this correspondence is a bijection.\n\n2006-10-12\n\nBenjamin Braun, Mike Develin\n\n# • INFO • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\nEhrhart Polynomial Roots and Stanley's Non-negativity Theorem\n\nPublished in Integer points in polyhedra--geometry, number theory, representation theory, algebra, optimization, statistics, 67--78, Contemp. Math., 452, Amer. Math. Soc., Providence, RI, 2008 • View Publication • BIB\n\nStanley's non-negativity theorem is at the heart of many of the results in Ehrhart theory. In this paper, we analyze the root behavior of general polynomials satisfying the conditions of Stanley's theorem and compare this to the known root behavior of Ehrhart polynomials. We provide a possible counterexample to a conjecture of the second author, M. Beck, J. De Loera, J. Pfeifle, and R. Stanley, and contribute some experimental data as well.\n\n2006-05-18 v2\n\nMike Develin, Josephine Yu\n\n# • INFO • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\nTropical polytopes and cellular resolutions\n\nPublished in Experimental Mathematics 16 (2007), no. 3, 277--291 • View Publication • BIB\n\nTropical polytopes are images of polytopes in an affine space over the Puiseux series field under the degree map. This viewpoint gives rise to a family of cellular resolutions of monomial ideals which generalize the hull complex of Bayer and Sturmfels, instances of which improve upon the hull resolution in the sense of being smaller. We also suggest a new definition of a face of a tropical polytope, which has nicer properties than previous definitions; we give examples and provide many conjectures and directions for further research in this area.\n\nalgebraic geometry phylogenetic simplicial complex tree\n\n2003-09-13\n\nMike Develin\n\n# • INFO • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\nMaximal triangulations of a regular prism\n\nPublished • View Publication • BIB\n\nIn this paper, we resolve two conjectures of De Loera, Santos, and Takeuchi in the affirmative, computing the maximal size of any regular triangulation of the $n$-prism and $n$-antiprism.\n\n2003-08-28\n\nMike Develin, Seth Sullivant\n\n# • INFO • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\nMarkov bases of binary graph models\n\nPublished • View Publication • BIB\n\nThis paper is concerned with the topological invariant of a graph given by the maximum degree of a Markov basis element for the corresponding graph model for binary contingency tables. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.d.umn.edu/~jgallian/progbib.html)\nciteturn1search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Research advisers: Mike Develin*, Stephen Hartke* ... Phil Matchett, Operations on well-covered graphs and the roller-coaster conjecture, The Electronic Journal of Combinatorics, 11 (2004) R45, 17 pages. ... Melody Chan, The maximum distinguishing number of a group, The Electronic Journal of Combinatorics, 13(1) R70 2006 (8 pages). ... Yakov Berchenko-Kogan, Minimal product sets sizes in nonabelian groups, Journal of Number Theory, 132 (2012) 2316-2335. ... Ryan Alweiss, Asymptotic results on Klazar set partition avoidance, Discrete Mathematics and Theoretical Computer Science, 19(2) (2018) 8 pp. arXiv:1608.02279\n\n### 2001 - Funded by NSF/NSA/UMD\n\nStudent Participants: Kelli Carlson, Andy Cotton, Geir Helleloid, Elena Grigorescu, Kate Ponto,\nJan Siwanowicz, Phil Matchett, Joe Rabinoff\nRese